# Without this file, the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` bakes these into the image.
# Two real problems that solves:
#  1. .env holds the real admin password - it would end up in an image layer
#     even though it's correctly gitignored. env_file: in docker-compose.yml
#     supplies it at RUNTIME from the host, so the image never needs a copy.
#  2. data/ is 180+ JPEGs plus birds.db - all of it is volume-mounted at
#     runtime (./data:/app/data), so copying it in just bloats the image
#     with a stale duplicate that gets shadowed by the mount anyway.
.env
data/

# Not needed inside the image
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.syno.tar
